{
  "id": "web-dev-176",
  "title": "Node.js Third-Party Modules - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Third-party modules are external libraries installed via </span><a href=\"#/article/c/c-471\"><span>npm</span></a><span> that extend Node.js functionality, such as handling </span><a href=\"#/article/networking/networking-081\"><span>HTTP</span></a><span> requests and other complex tasks.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Not included by default in Node.js and must be installed manually.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Installed and managed using npm, which handles dependencies and updates.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Provide ready-made solutions for routing, authentication, database integration, and other </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-754\"><span>backend</span></a><span> tasks.</span></li></ul><h2 id=\"installing-and-using-thirdparty-modules\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Installing and Using Third-Party Modules</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Node.js uses npm, the world’s largest software registry, to manage third-party packages. To install A module is straightforward; you just need to give the command \"npm install express\".</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-113003\" height=\"182\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-1.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113015211364/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113003.jpg 616w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113015211364/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113003-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113015211364/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113003-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113015211364/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113003-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"616\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>This command installs the popular express web framework and adds it to the project's</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2491\"><span> node_modules</span></a><span> directory. To use the installed module you just simply need to give the \"require\" command .</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"false\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">app.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">express</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'express'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">express</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">app</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'/'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">req</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">send</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'Hello Martin!'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">app</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">listen</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">3000</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'Server running on port 3000'</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>When you start running your server on port no 3000 you  will see output Hello Martin!</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-113133\" height=\"152\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-2.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113145902468/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113133.jpg 372w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113145902468/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113133-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113145902468/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113133-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113145902468/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113133-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"372\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"popular-thirdparty-modules\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Popular Third-Party Modules</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Here are some widely adopted third-party modules:</span></p><h3 id=\"express-web-framework\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>1. Express </span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-034\"><span>Express</span></a><span> is a fast, minimalist web framework for </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-008\"><span>Node.js</span></a><span> that simplifies the process of building </span><a href=\"#/article/java/java-1508\"><span>web applications</span></a><span> and </span><a href=\"#/article/python/python-605\"><span>APIs</span></a><span>. It provides robust </span><a href=\"#/article/networking/networking-033\"><span>routing</span></a><span>, </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2492\"><span>middleware </span></a><span>support, and </span><a href=\"#/article/java/java-1362\"><span>HTTP </span></a><span>utility methods.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"false\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">app.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">express</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'express'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">app</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">express</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">app</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'/'</span><span class=\"p\">,(</span><span class=\"nx\">req</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">)=&gt;{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">send</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'Hello from Express'</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">app</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">listen</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">8080</span><span class=\"p\">,()=&gt;{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'app created successfully'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p\">})</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-113535\" height=\"72\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-3.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113548235130/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113535.jpg 537w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113548235130/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113535-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113548235130/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113535-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303113548235130/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113535-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"537\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"mongoose\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>2. Mongoose </span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2493\"><span>Mongoose</span></a><span> is an Object Data Modeling (ODM) library for </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-016\"><span>MongoDB</span></a><span> and Node.js. It provides a straightforward way to define </span><a href=\"#/article/sql/sql-149\"><span>schemas</span></a><span> and interact with MongoDB using</span><a href=\"#/article/java/java-1440\"><span> JavaScript objects.</span></a></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"false\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">index.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">mongoose</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'mongoose'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">mongoose</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">connect</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'mongodb://localhost:27017/testDB'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">userSchema</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ow\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">mongoose</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Schema</span><span class=\"p\">({</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nx\">name</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">String</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nx\">age</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Number</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">User</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">mongoose</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">model</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'User'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">userSchema</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">newUser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ow\">new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">User</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">name</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'Alex'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">age</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">25</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">});</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">newUser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">save</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"nx\">then</span><span class=\"p\">(()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'User saved!'</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output: </strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-113940\" height=\"72\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-4.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114009705618/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113940.jpg 563w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114009705618/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113940-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114009705618/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113940-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114009705618/Screenshot-2026-03-03-113940-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"563\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>You can check the data in the database ie. username , user id, user age etc.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-114337\" height=\"417\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-5.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114349635543/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114337.jpg 813w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114349635543/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114337-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114349635543/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114337-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114349635543/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114337-300.jpg 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114349635543/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114337-660.jpg 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114349635543/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114337-768.jpg 768w\" width=\"813\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"axios\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>3. Axios </span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2494\"><span>Axios</span></a><span> is a promise-based HTTP client for Node.js and the</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-043\"><span> browser</span></a><span>. It simplifies making</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2495\"><span> HTTP requests</span></a><span>, handling responses, and managing errors.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"false\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">axios.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">axios</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'axios'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">axios</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1'</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">then</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">response</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">response</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">data</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">error</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">error</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">error</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-114812\" height=\"216\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-6.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114825391816/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114812.jpg 780w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114825391816/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114812-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114825391816/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114812-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114825391816/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114812-300.jpg 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114825391816/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114812-660.jpg 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303114825391816/Screenshot-2026-03-03-114812-768.jpg 768w\" width=\"780\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"lodash-utiity-library\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>4. lodash</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/java/java-312\"><span>Lodash </span></a><span>is a utility library that provides helpful functions for manipulating </span><a href=\"#/article/dsa/dsa-1047\"><span>arrays, </span></a><a href=\"#/article/java/java-1440\"><span>objects,</span></a><a href=\"#/article/java/java-235\"><span>strings,</span></a><span> and more—making</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-006\"><span> JavaScript </span></a><span>code cleaner and more readable.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"false\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">lodash.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'lodash'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">numbers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">10</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">8</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">3</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">sorted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">sortBy</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">numbers</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">sorted</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><br><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-115008\" height=\"57\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-7.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115024010361/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115008.jpg 563w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115024010361/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115008-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115024010361/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115008-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115024010361/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115008-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"563\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"dotenv\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>5. dotenv</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2496\"><span>dotenv</span></a><span> is a zero-dependency module that loads </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2497\"><span>environment variables</span></a><span> from a .env file into </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2498\"><span>process.env.</span></a><span> It helps manage configuration settings securely and separately from code.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"false\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">app.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"cpp\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-cpp\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">'</span><span class=\"n\">dotenv</span><span class=\"err\">'</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"n\">config</span><span class=\"p\">();</span>\n<span class=\"n\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PORT</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// 4000</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel>\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">.env</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"nx\">PORT</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">4000</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-115343\" height=\"73\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-8.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115359611462/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115343.jpg 897w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115359611462/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115343-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115359611462/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115343-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115359611462/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115343-300.jpg 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115359611462/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115343-660.jpg 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303115359611462/Screenshot-2026-03-03-115343-768.jpg 768w\" width=\"897\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Note:</strong></b><span> You should have</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2499\"><span> .env file </span></a><span>in the same folder  have  Port no . i.e PORT= 4000</span></p></blockquote><h3 id=\"nodemon\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>6. Nodemon</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-2500\"><span>Nodemon</span></a><span> is  a development utility that automatically restarts  your </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-170\"><span>Node.js Application</span></a><span> whenever file change. It is very useful during development to avoid  manually stopping and restarting the</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1426\"><span> server </span></a><span>after every change.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">fsappend.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'fs'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">// Append data to a file</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">fs</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">appendFile</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'demo.txt'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'New data added\\n'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">err</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">err</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">error</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Error writing to file:\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">err</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Data added in my file Successfully\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Installation : </strong></b><span>To install nodemon you need to run this command.</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-120018\" height=\"131\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-9.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303120037601672/Screenshot-2026-03-03-120018.jpg 597w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303120037601672/Screenshot-2026-03-03-120018-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303120037601672/Screenshot-2026-03-03-120018-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303120037601672/Screenshot-2026-03-03-120018-300.jpg 300w\" width=\"597\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>To run the command using nodemon</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Screenshot-2026-03-03-121003\" height=\"192\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-10.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121021047091/Screenshot-2026-03-03-121003.jpg 695w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121021047091/Screenshot-2026-03-03-121003-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121021047091/Screenshot-2026-03-03-121003-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121021047091/Screenshot-2026-03-03-121003-300.jpg 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121021047091/Screenshot-2026-03-03-121003-660.jpg 660w\" width=\"695\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"jsonwebtoken\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>7. Jsonwebtoken</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"#/article/python/python-610\"><span>Jsonwebtoken (or jwt) </span></a><span>is a module that enables you to generate and verify </span><a href=\"#/article/python/python-610\"><span>JSON Web Tokens</span></a><span>, commonly used for implementing secure authentication in</span><a href=\"#/article/python/python-605\"><span> APIs.</span></a></p><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"false\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">jsonwebtoken.js</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"javascript\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-javascript\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">jwt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'jsonwebtoken'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">token</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">jwt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">sign</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">username</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'Martin'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'secretKey'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'JWT:'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">token</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">decoded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">jwt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">verify</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">token</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'secretKey'</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s1\">'Decoded:'</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">decoded</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"json\" height=\"71\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/web-dev-176-img-11.jpg\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121615101096/json.jpg 1098w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121615101096/json-100.jpg 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121615101096/json-200.jpg 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121615101096/json-300.jpg 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121615101096/json-660.jpg 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121615101096/json-768.jpg 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20260303121615101096/json-1024.jpg 1024w\" width=\"1098\"><figcaption> </figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"advantages-of-thirdparty-modules\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Advantages of Third-Party Modules</span></h2><ul><li value=\"1\"><b><strong>Faster Development:</strong></b><span> Reduces development time by providing pre-built functionality.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Reliability:</strong></b><span> Well-maintained modules receive regular updates and community support.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>Security:</strong></b><span> Popular modules are frequently patched to address known vulnerabilities.</span></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>Maintainability:</strong></b><span> Promotes modular, reusable code and simplifies application maintenance.</span></li></ul></div>",
  "textContent": "Third-party modules are external libraries installed via npm that extend Node.js functionality, such as handling HTTP requests and other complex tasks.Not included by default in Node.js and must be installed manually.Installed and managed using npm, which handles dependencies and updates.Provide ready-made solutions for routing, authentication, database integration, and other backend tasks.Installing and Using Third-Party ModulesNode.js uses npm, the world’s largest software registry, to manage third-party packages. To install A module is straightforward; you just need to give the command \"npm install express\". This command installs the popular express web framework and adds it to the project's node_modules directory. To use the installed module you just simply need to give the \"require\" command .\n            app.js\n\n    const express = require('express');\nconst app = express();\napp.get('/', (req, res) => {\n  res.send('Hello Martin!');\n});\napp.listen(3000, () => console.log('Server running on port 3000'));\n\nWhen you start running your server on port no 3000 you  will see output Hello Martin!Output: Popular Third-Party ModulesHere are some widely adopted third-party modules:1. Express Express is a fast, minimalist web framework for Node.js that simplifies the process of building web applications and APIs. It provides robust routing, middleware support, and HTTP utility methods.\n            app.js\n\n    const express= require('express');\nconst app= express();\napp.get('/',(req,res)=>{\n    res.send('Hello from Express')\n});\napp.listen(8080,()=>{\n    console.log('app created successfully');\n})\n\nOutput: 2. Mongoose Mongoose is an Object Data Modeling (ODM) library for MongoDB and Node.js. It provides a straightforward way to define schemas and interact with MongoDB using JavaScript objects.\n            index.js\n\n    const mongoose = require('mongoose');\nmongoose.connect('mongodb://localhost:27017/testDB');\nconst userSchema = new mongoose.Schema({\n  name: String,\n  age: Number\n});\nconst User = mongoose.model('User', userSchema);\nconst newUser = new User({ name: 'Alex', age: 25 });\nnewUser.save().then(() => console.log('User saved!'));\n\nOutput:  You can check the data in the database ie. username , user id, user age etc. 3. Axios Axios is a promise-based HTTP client for Node.js and the browser. It simplifies making HTTP requests, handling responses, and managing errors.\n            axios.js\n\n    const axios = require('axios');\naxios.get('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1')\n  .then(response => {\n    console.log(response.data);\n  })\n  .catch(error => {\n    console.error(error);\n  });\n\nOutput: 4. lodashLodash is a utility library that provides helpful functions for manipulating arrays, objects,strings, and more—making JavaScript code cleaner and more readable.\n            lodash.js\n\n    const _ = require('lodash');\nconst numbers = [10, 5, 8, 3];\nconst sorted = _.sortBy(numbers);\nconsole.log(sorted); \n\nOutput: 5. dotenvdotenv is a zero-dependency module that loads environment variables from a .env file into process.env. It helps manage configuration settings securely and separately from code.\n            app.js\n\n    require('dotenv').config();\nconsole.log(process.env.PORT); // 4000\n\n\n            .env\n\n    PORT=4000\n\nOutput: Note: You should have .env file in the same folder  have  Port no . i.e PORT= 40006. NodemonNodemon is  a development utility that automatically restarts  your Node.js Application whenever file change. It is very useful during development to avoid  manually stopping and restarting the server after every change.\n            fsappend.js\n\n    const fs = require('fs');\n\n// Append data to a file\nfs.appendFile('demo.txt', 'New data added\\n', (err) => {\n    if (err) {\n        console.error(\"Error writing to file:\", err);\n    } else {\n        console.log(\"Data added in my file Successfully\");\n    }\n});\n\nInstallation : To install nodemon you need to run this command. To run the command using nodemon 7. JsonwebtokenJsonwebtoken (or jwt) is a module that enables you to generate and verify JSON Web Tokens, commonly used for implementing secure authentication in APIs.\n            jsonwebtoken.js\n\n    const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\nconst token = jwt.sign({ username: 'Martin' }, 'secretKey');\nconsole.log('JWT:', token);\nconst decoded = jwt.verify(token, 'secretKey');\nconsole.log('Decoded:', decoded);\n\nOutput: Advantages of Third-Party ModulesFaster Development: Reduces development time by providing pre-built functionality.Reliability: Well-maintained modules receive regular updates and community support.Security: Popular modules are frequently patched to address known vulnerabilities.Maintainability: Promotes modular, reusable code and simplifies application maintenance.",
